Approval Note (Product Compliance Review)
Ticket No.: {ticket}  Submitted by: Content Security Team  Review date: {date}
Product: household formaldehyde detector, listed in batch {batch}, store {site}
Issue description: The detail page claims “detection accuracy 100%, absolutely accurate, never false alarms,” and the main image also bears “certification by a national-level testing institution.” The merchant provided only a photocopy of a 2023 self-submitted testing authorization letter; the report number is inconsistent with the number the merchant entered in the backend, and the institution name cannot be found in the searchable directory.
Handling recommendation: False advertising is established. Within the past 90 days, this store has already been given 1 warning for absolute wording such as “lowest price across the entire network” ({date}, handling ticket {ticket}); under Article 5.3 of the detailed rules, a 2nd instance of false or absolute advertising by the same store within 90 days is recorded as a demotion. This disposition is a demotion, not a delisting.
