From: Content Governance Team-{site}
To: Merchant Operations-{customer}
Subject: [Disposition Notice] {ticket} Product Title Contains Absolute Terms and Efficacy Claims
Body:
During the inspection on {date}, the detail page of the product on sale {order_no} was found to contain the following statements:
1. The title states “Lowest price across the entire internet, national-level certification, boosts immunity, takes effect in 7 days”;
2. Screen 3 of the detail page states “Effective rate 100%, no cases of ineffective feedback”;
3. The product is actually an ordinary solid beverage and has no health food approval number; the test report provided by the merchant (No. {batch}) covers only total bacterial count.
Among these, “lowest across the entire internet,” “100%,” and “takes effect in 7 days” are absolute terms and unsubstantiated efficacy claims. Under Article 3.1 of the Content Violation Disposition Rules: it is the first occurrence, the page has had no transaction disputes in the recent 90 days, and the store has no similar violations in its history; all three conditions are met, so the disposition level is ranking reduction, i.e., blocking from search and recommendation slots for 7 days, without direct delisting.
In addition: the contract clause dispute over the supplier’s temporary 8% price increase that {customer} asked about last week has been handed over to procurement; there is no need to forward it again in this email; the damaged logistics item for {case_id} was also handled before {time}.
The merchant is requested to revise the title and detail page within 48 hours; if overdue, it will be escalated to delisting.

[Original consumer complaint]
Complainant: {customer}
Complaint time: {date} {time}
Order No.: {order_no}
Product: children's insulated cup 500ml ({batch})
Complaint content: After receiving the goods, I felt it did not look like a genuine product—a “three-no product”, right? I did not see manufacturer information on the bottom of the cup. I request a return and threefold compensation. In addition, the logistics dispatcher I asked last week said the parcel was held for 2 days at the {site} transit center; this should also be counted.

[Review verification record]
1. Merchant qualifications retrieved: business license, product quality inspection report (No. {batch}), and 3C certification are all within their validity periods;
2. The laser engraving on the bottom of the cup is the manufacturer name and executive standard; because the shooting angle did not capture it, the merchant has been asked to retake the main image;
3. This product has had 1 complaint in the past 180 days (i.e., this one), with no quality-related work orders;
4. The price is 129 yuan, consistent with the brand's official price of 129 yuan; there is no abnormally low price;
5. No explicit evidence of trademark infringement, prohibited sales, false advertising, or safety hazards was found.
Conclusion: The complaint is not established; the product is released and no action is taken; the merchant is only reminded to supplement the main image.
Remarks: The contract clause dispute over the supplier's temporary 5% price increase goes through the procurement process; {ticket} is another {device} work order and is unrelated to this order.

Work order text {ticket} (submitted on {date}, source: inspection)
Product link: {order_no}, category listed under “Household small appliances”; what is actually sold is soft contact lenses (contact lenses), and the detail page states “daily disposable, 30-piece pack, can be worn continuously for 12 hours.”
Verification process:
1. This category belongs to Class III medical devices and must have both a Medical Device Business License and a product registration certificate number;
2. The merchant qualification field is empty; only one business license was uploaded, and its business scope does not include medical device sales;
3. The backend sent three requests to submit the missing documents ({date}, {date}, {date}); the merchant did not submit them on any occasion and replied “other stores sell it this way too”;
4. The page does not mark any contraindications or wearing warnings.
Conclusion and recommendation: It is a prohibited sale or missing qualifications; delist the product immediately, and record one serious violation against the store.
One additional note: what a logistics dispatcher asked about yesterday was the arrival time for {batch}; it has nothing to do with this work order, so do not mix up the orders.

