From: Content Review Team-{customer}
To: Merchant Operations-{site}
Subject: Review of delisting for {case_id} product

Body: The men's cushioned running shoes (product number {order_no}) listed by merchant {site} on {date} had the title "same style as a certain sports brand" and the main image directly used that brand's registered trademark graphic. The brand's agency law firm submitted an infringement complaint on {date}, with an appraisal report stating that the submitted sample is a counterfeit product and not authorized production, and that all 3 authenticity codes on the shoe tongue cannot be verified. The authorization chain submitted by the merchant contains only a distribution agreement expiring in 2021, covering apparel, and explicitly excluding footwear. In addition, you do not need to worry about the refund progress of the order {ticket}; customer service has already handled it. On our side, we lean toward handling it as counterfeit; please confirm the disposition action.

Monthly cumulative violation assessment table (store {site}):
1) {date} The product description used absolute terms such as "national-level certification" and "absolutely safe", 6 points;
2) {date} Sold Class III in vitro diagnostic reagents without filing, 12 points;
3) {date} The main image used another party's registered trademark, 3 points.
Cumulative total this month: 21 points. Per Rule 6.1, a cumulative total of ≥15 points in a calendar month triggers delisting, and the action is delisting; the primary violation type is the item with the highest score among the sub-items. In addition, the logistics complaint for order {order_no} of this store is being followed up by Customer Service Team 3 and is unrelated to this assessment.

Review note {ticket}
Product: cotton-linen four-piece set. The material composition is 55% linen and 45% cotton, consistent with the composition table on the page; the washing labels are complete; the title is “Skin-friendly and breathable, suitable for all seasons,” with no absolute wording; the main image matches the actual product and contains no brand logos or third-party trademark elements. In the description, “polyester-cotton” was written as “strip cotton,” which is a typo and does not constitute a promotional violation. Determination: no violations found; release.
Note: The duty roster for {date} has been sent to the group; please confirm before {time}.

Risk product screening record {date}
Link {batch}-C09 sells “cold sparkler sticks, handheld fireworks”; sales volume 3120 items. The shipping location has no Fireworks and Firecrackers Business (Retail) License. The product details state “can be lit indoors, suitable for children's birthdays,” and buyer reviews include 6 photos of children holding lit sparklers. The platform's prohibited-sales rules explicitly prohibit the entire fireworks and firecracker category; unlicensed merchants are all delisted and deducted 12 points.
(The 190 links screened in the same batch are all ordinary stationery and passed. The overtime application for {case_id} has been approved.)

Content review receipt {date}
The product {batch}-B22 sun-protection clothing detail page claims “100% UV blocking, UPF100+”; the test report provided by the merchant shows a measured UPF value of 38, and the report expired 8 months ago. The claimed value does not match the measured value, constituting exaggerated advertising; the merchant has 1 previous similar reminder record within 90 days. This is not a first violation. Under the rules, this violation is recorded as 2 points; together with the previous 1 point, the cumulative total is 3 points. The interval [3,4] corresponds to a traffic reduction.
(For the category commission issue raised by {case_id}, please follow the finance process.)

Search term violation review {batch}
The store filled in another party's registered trademark "XX Aurora" in the title and keyword fields as a traffic-driving keyword, while actually selling its own brand "YY Aurora". The product itself is not a counterfeit, nor does it use another party's packaging. The rights holder's complaint is about confusing use of keywords. First violation: per the rules, a first keyword infringement violation records 2 points, cumulative 2 points; the interval [1,2] corresponds to traffic reduction, and the keyword must be deleted within 24 hours.
(Also: the influencer live-stream schedule {case_id} asked about has been sent to the group.)

